    "created_at": "2020-05-10T16:05:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-10T16:05:53Z",
    "body": "I confirmed that this is a quirk IE6+/Chrome (on Windows only) have. They do it for both `d:/foo` and `d:\\foo`. In fact, they do it for any a-z scheme. IE6 also does it for a 0-9 or -/+ scheme; I'll consider those to be bugs. (Firefox's address bar quirk is only with a backslash, not a forward slash.)\r\n\r\nThoughts on only adopting this when a backslash is used? Or should we add a platform-specific quirk here similar to https://w3c.github.io/FileAPI/#convert-line-endings-to-native and make single-scheme URLs impossible forever on that platform?\r\n\r\ncc @sleevi @valenting @achristensen07 @jasnell ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
