    "body": "@hayatoito thoughts on this?\r\n\r\nI would be okay with treating `[a-zA-Z]:\\` in a special way, in particular because `\\` is invalid when not percent-encoded, but I would strongly prefer not doing this for `[a-zA-Z]:/`, as it seems like too much of a breaking change from expected URL semantics.",
